@startuml
title Login and Role-Based Access
actor User
participant "Angular login" as UI
participant "AuthController" as C
participant "AuthenticationService" as A
participant "UserRepository" as R
participant "JWT signer" as J
User -> UI : Enter credentials
UI -> C : POST /api/v1/auth/login
C -> A : Authenticate
A -> R : Find user by normalized email
R --> A : User and BCrypt hash
alt User not found, invalid password or disabled
  A --> C : Generic authentication failure
  C --> UI : 401 error envelope (1001)
else Valid credentials
  A -> J : Issue RS256 JWT; expires in 900 seconds
  J --> A : JWT with subject and role
  A --> C : Token + safe user profile
  C --> UI : 200 envelope (error_code 0)
  UI -> UI : Keep token in memory
  UI --> User : Route by role
end
note over UI, J
Every protected API validates JWT, current enabled/role state and ownership.
Replicas share issuer/audience and compatible key configuration.
Reload / expiry / sign-out requires login; no refresh token.
Frontend route guards are not authorization.
end note
@enduml
